# RetrofitTrust Birmingham — Core Rules

MSc AI dissertation PoC at BCU. Title: **Intelligent Urban Decision-Making Framework Using AI, Blockchain and Digital Twins.**

## Non-negotiable stack
- **Ranking model:** LightGBM or XGBoost + SHAP TreeExplainer — NOT deep learning
- **Anomaly detection:** PyOD AutoEncoder + Isolation Forest ensemble — quarantine/flag, never silent delete
- **Dashboard:** Streamlit + geopandas + Plotly choropleth — must include write-back loop via SQLite
- **Ledger:** Python hashlib SHA-256 hash-chain — NOT real blockchain; synthetic grant data labelled "SYNTHETIC DATA"
- **Backend:** FastAPI with `/rank`, `/explain`, `/ledger/append`, `/ledger/verify`
- **Layout:** Cookiecutter Data Science v2; `data/raw` is immutable; logic in `src/retrofittrust/`

## Build order
1. Data pipeline + join on 2021 LSOA (EPC Birmingham-filtered, IMD 2025, Census TS054 + Central Heating)
2. Anomaly screening (feeds preprocessing)
3. LightGBM + SHAP
4. Streamlit dashboard (static first, then write-back)
5. Ledger standalone, then FastAPI integration

## Academic priorities
- End-to-end integration loop (twin → AI → ledger → write-back) matters more than polish
- Acknowledge limitations: ecological fallacy (LSOA IMD), EPC performance gap, SHAP correlated-feature caveat
- British English; fixed random seeds (`SEED = 42`); pin requirements.txt versions

## Do NOT build without RJ approval
Real blockchain, 3D twin, deep learning core model, production auth, IoT streaming, time-series forecasting.
